    pr_ref:  # 25ab
    description: "Repro (dev 77cca016e9): record Point(int X,int Y) { public int M() { return Helper(); } int Helper() {...} } plus class Other { public int Helper() {...} } -> symbols M, Helper (no Point, no Point. qualifier), and calls M -> Other.Helper. Consequence: record methods are unfindable by qualified name, and their calls are attributed to an unrelated class, so Point.Helper looks dead and Other.Helper gains a false caller. Likely cause: the C# analyzer's enclosing-class walk (_get_enclosing_class) omits record_declaration; the type-emission path probably omits it too. Analogue of WI-fonaz (PHP traits/enums) fixed in PR #2092; check record struct as well."  # 25ab
    fields: {}  # 25ab
